{"created": "2026-09-14T16:06:18.650630+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-14T16:06:19.181512+00:00", "id": 22722081, "conceptrecid": "22722080", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722081", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722080", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722081", "metadata": {"title": "HNN extensions and inner homogeneity of group representations over commutative rings", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722081", "publication_date": "2026-09-12", "description": "<p>Let \\(R\\) be a nonzero commutative ring. Every \\(R\\)-representation \\((G,V)\\) embeds in \\((\\Gamma,W)\\) with \\[\\ker\\bigl(\\Gamma\\to\\operatorname{Aut}_R(W)\\bigr)=1,\\qquad |\\Gamma|,|W|\\le\\max\\{\\aleph_0,|R|,|G|,|V|\\},\\] such that every isomorphism between finitely generated subrepresentations is induced by \\((g\\mapsto tgt^{-1},\\,w\\mapsto tw)\\) for some \\(t\\in\\Gamma\\). A local HNN construction realizes arbitrary subrepresentation isomorphisms by adjoining the corresponding linear relations to an induced module. Injectivity follows from the boundary map of a tree of modules, with no splitting or projectivity assumption. The field case answers Kourovka Problem 17.101.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Jayadevan, Achyuth", "affiliation": "Manipal Institute of Technology, MAHE", "orcid": "0009-0008-8745-4078"}], "keywords": ["Kourovka Problem 17.101", "Group representations", "HNN extensions", "Homogeneous representations", "Commutative rings", "Lean 4"], "version": "1.0.0", "references": ["E. V. Aladova, A. A. Gvaramiya and B. I. Plotkin, Logic in representations of groups, Algebra and Logic 51 (2012), 1\u201327. https://doi.org/10.1007/s10469-012-9167-8 Russian original: Algebra i Logika 51 (2012), 3\u201340. https://www.mathnet.ru/al520", "W. Dicks, Mayer\u2013Vietoris presentations over colimits of rings, Proc. London Math. Soc. (3) 34 (1977), no. 3, 557\u2013576. https://doi.org/10.1112/plms/s3-34.3.557", "W. Dicks, The HNN construction for rings, J. Algebra 81 (1983), no. 2, 434\u2013487. https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693(83)90198-9", "G. Higman, B. H. Neumann and H. Neumann, Embedding theorems for groups, J. London Math. Soc. 24 (1949), no. 4, 247\u2013254. https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/s1-24.4.247", "O. H. Kegel, Examples of highly transitive permutation groups, Rend. Sem. Mat. Univ. Padova 63 (1980), 295\u2013300.", "E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st ed., Problem 17.101. https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v46"], "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Achxy/k-17-101", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "lean", "title": {"en": "Lean"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22722080"}}]}}, "title": "HNN extensions and inner homogeneity of group representations over commutative rings", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722081", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722081", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722081?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722081", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722081", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22722081", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722081/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722080", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722080", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722080", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22722080", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722081/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722081/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722081/files", "media_files": "https://zenod